                <pb facs="0317" n="219" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg219"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Pekin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-10-24"><hi rendition="#italic">October 24,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Conger reports Earl Li’s statement that Emperor has given no intimation of
                    returning, and that no one can speak for him.</p>
                <p>May have to accept as sufficient proof of Imperial authority the punishment of
                    designated leaders and restoration of order, without Emperor’s early
                    return.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
